{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351582-worse-than-it-looks","id":1351582,"title":"Worse Than It Looks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-28T21:09:13-08:00","id":1351582,"title":"Worse Than It Looks","content":"I've decided to spend the weekend brushing up on new games and am in the process of reading the Trinity core. I have no familiarity with 1st Edition, but I know the Storypath System was a substantial undertaking with new mechanics not present in the previous edition. On p. 216, Worse Than It Looks reads: &quot;Once per combat, spend a point of Inspiration to increase the damage dealt to an antagonist by one Health Box.&quot;<br /> <br /> Am I correct in thinking that this language is a throwback to the 1st Edition rules (I've so been there)? If so, what is the intention here? Should this be an additional Injury (or reduced cost of the Critical Stunt), an Enhancement, or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T23:02:11-08:00","id":1351599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351582-worse-than-it-looks#post1351582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I correct in thinking that this language is a throwback to the 1st Edition rules (I've so been there)?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was no core Trinity Continuum rulebook last time around, just \u00c6on, Aberrant, and Adventure!. This is more likely a remnant of one of the four major revisions of Storypath we went through during development. There were a bunch of rogue references that made it through until fairly late in development.<br /> <br /> In this case: you normally get one optional &quot;free&quot; Injury Stunt with a successful attack, and can then spend four successes to get a Critical Injury Stunt, for a total of two injuries. <i>Worse Than It Looks</i> would grant you one additional free Injury prior to the Critical stunt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T04:39:02-08:00","id":1351629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351582-worse-than-it-looks?p=1351599#post1351599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was no core Trinity Continuum rulebook last time around, just \u00c6on, Aberrant, and Adventure!. This is more likely a remnant of one of the four major revisions of Storypath we went through during development. There were a bunch of rogue references that made it through until fairly late in development.<br /> <br /> In this case: you normally get one optional &quot;free&quot; Injury Stunt with a successful attack, and can then spend four successes to get a Critical Injury Stunt, for a total of two injuries. <i>Worse Than It Looks</i> would grant you one additional free Injury prior to the Critical stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been <i>there</i>, too. Sneaky, sneaky manuscript gremlins. Thanks, Ian!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}